# Files at the root of this package that must NOT be linked into $HOME.
#
# The repo is flat — its root *is* the macOS package — so repo bookkeeping and
# the common/ submodule sit alongside the dotfiles and have to be excluded by
# name. GNU Stow's default ignore list already covers some of this, but a
# package-local .stow-local-ignore REPLACES that default list rather than adding
# to it, so everything has to be spelled out here.
#
# Patterns are regexes and must satisfy two consumers:
#   * GNU Stow anchors each pattern at both ends, matching the basename when the
#     pattern has no slash in it.
#   * common/stow.sh searches unanchored against the path with a leading slash.
# Slash-free basename patterns behave correctly under both.

# Repo bookkeeping
README\.md
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitattributes
\.gitmodules
\.stow-local-ignore
\.DS_Store

# The shared package, mounted here as a submodule. It is stowed in its own
# right (it is the other package), so linking it from here would put a
# ~/common symlink in $HOME and duplicate every file underneath it.
common

# Names this repo's package to stow.sh, which otherwise cannot tell whether the
# directory above the submodule is a per-OS package or just wherever the
# checkout happens to live. Not config, so never linked.
\.stow-os
